<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Cristóvão da Gama</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1516–<a href="/years/1542">1542</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> · Also known as Cristovao da Gama</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Cristóvão da Gama was a Portuguese commander, a son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vasco-da-gama">Vasco da Gama</a>, who led about 400 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/musket">musketeers</a> to support the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ethiopian-empire">Ethiopian Empire</a> against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/adal-sultanate">Adal Sultanate</a> in 1541. He won several engagements before being captured and executed by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ahmad-ibn-ibrahim-al-ghazi">Ahmad ibn Ibrahim al-Ghazi</a> in 1542. His surviving troops helped Emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/galawdewos">Galawdewos</a> defeat and kill Ahmad at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-wayna-daga">Wayna Daga</a> in 1543.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/cristovao-da-gama.jpg" alt="Cristóvão da Gama" width="271" height="323" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Brian Snelson · CC BY 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Crist%C3%B3v%C3%A3o_da_Gama_-_Padr%C3%A3o_dos_Descobrimentos.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
